  "title": "Evil-Repelling Prayers and Supplicatory Amulets",
  "data": "Dua against Loneliness\nTo not feel lonely, neither at night nor in daytime, recite:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ وَتَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّتَوَكَّلُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ حَسْبُهٗ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَالِغُ اَمْرِهٖ قَدْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لِكُلِّ شَيْئٍ قَدْرًا اَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِىْ فِىْ كَنَفِكَ وَفِىْ جِوَارِكَ وَاجْعَلْنِىْ فِىْ اَمَانِكَ وَفِىْ مَنْعِكَ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI WA TAWAKKALTU A'LALLAAH, INNAHU MAY YATAWAKKAL A'LALLAAHI FAHUWA HASBUH, INNALLAAHA BAALIGHU AMRIH, QAD JA-A'LALLAAHU LI-KULLI SHAY-IN QADRAA, ALLAAHUMMAJ-A'LNEE FEE KANAFIKA WA FEE JIWAARIKA WAJ-A'LNEE FEE AMAANIKA WA FEE MAN-I'K\nIn the name of Allah, and by Allah, and I have placed my trust in Allah; verily whoever places his trust in Allah, He suffices him — verily Allah brings about His purpose; Allah has appointed for everything its measure. O Allah, place me under Your protection and in Your shelter, and place me in Your safekeeping and Your defense.",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua for a Night Alone\nWhen spending a night alone in a house or a room, recite [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) and this supplication:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اٰنِسْ وَحْشَتِىْ وَاٰمِنْ رَوْعَتِىْ وَاَعِنِّىْ عَلٰى وَحْدَتِىْ\nALLAAHUMMA AANIS WAHSHATEE WA AAMIN RAW-A'TEE WA A'INNEE A'LAA WAHDATEE\nO Allah, ease my sense of isolation, secure me from my fright, and aid me in my solitude.",
    "Protection of Hasan & Husayn\nRecite to seek protection for others, as the Holy Prophet (s) did for Imam al-Hasan and Imam al-Husayn (a):\nاُعِيْذُ كُمَا بِكَلِمَاتِ اللّٰهِ التَّاۤمَّةِ وَاَسْمَاۤئِهِ الْحُسْنٰى كُلِّهَا عَاۤمَّةً مِنْ شَرِّ السَّاۤمَّةِ وَالْهَاۤمَّةِ وَمِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ عَيْنٍ لَاۤمَّةٍ وَمِنْ شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ اِذَا حَسَدَ\nU'EEZU KUMAA BI-KALIMAATILLAAHIT TAAA-MMATI WA ASMAAA-IHIL HUSNAA KULLIHAA A'AAAMMATAM MIN SHARRIS SAAA-MMATI WAL HAAA-MMATI WA MIN SHARRI KULLI A'YNIL LAAA-MMATI WA MIN SHARRI HAASIDIN IZAA HASAD\nI seek refuge for you both in the perfect words of Allah and in all of His most beautiful names, altogether, from the evil of every venomous creature and every noxious creature, and from the evil of every touching eye, and from the evil of an envier when he envies."
  ],
  "merits": "Dua against Loneliness: It is reported that when a man complained to Imam al-Sadiq (a) about loneliness, the Imam (a) said: may I lead you to a prayer such that, if you say it, you will not feel lonely, neither at night nor in daytime? It is reported that a man used to say this supplicatory prayer for thirty years incessantly, but when he neglected it one night, he was stung by a scorpion that same night.\n\nProtection of Hasan & Husayn: Commenting, the Holy Prophet (s) added, \"Thus did (Prophet) Abraham use to repel evil from Ishmael and Isaac.\""
